      "id": 1,
      "text": "McDade was founded in 1869 to serve the Houston and Texas Central Railroad as it crossed northern Bastrop County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mountbonnell.info/beyond-austin-city-limits/mcdade"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s historic saloon, built in 1873, now houses the McDade Historical Society Museum and once hosted outlaws like Sam Bass and Wild Bill Longley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://bastropcountyhistorical.org/museum/mcdade-historical-society-museum/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Television star Gale Storm grew up in McDade, where her mother ran a millinery shop that supplied hats to the local community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McDade%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every fourth Monday, the McDade Historical Society meets at 7 p.m. to preserve local stories and organize events like Santa for the Kids and Trunk or Treat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://bastropcountyhistorical.org/museum/mcdade-historical-society-museum/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "McDade’s Captain Jesse Billingsley Memorial, a veteran of the Battle of San Jacinto, stands just across the street from the museum, honoring a local hero who lived his final years in town.",
